# Our changes to the upstream web app, applied in this order at build time by
# scripts/upstream/apply_patches.py. apps/web and packages stay identical to the
# pinned upstream release; the upstream check fails if any patch stops applying.
# Format: <patch file>  <one-line reason>
0001-seventwos-web-branding.patch  Seventwos names, links and help pages instead of Element ones
0002-remove-default-call-domain-and-help-links.patch  No default third-party video-call domain; drop help links that point at Element
0003-seventwos-service-defaults.patch  Default configuration uses only Seventwos services
0004-remove-unreachable-links.patch  Remove links that no longer resolve and the default video-call domain
0005-harden-translation-text.patch  Harden translation text handling
0006-carry-call-default-and-help-link-fixes.patch  No default video-call domain or third-party integration manager; Seventwos names and help link in the remaining config and toast
0007-point-help-links-at-existing-pages.patch  Help, logo and verification links point at seventwos.com pages that exist; drop the dead develop link
0008-carry-remaining-web-delta.patch  Fix a type error in the QR code test helper
